# Build context for apps/server/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile, both of which
# are built from the REPOSITORY ROOT — pnpm workspaces need the lockfile and every
# workspace manifest, so a context rooted at one app cannot resolve.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS WRITTEN IN BOTH FORMS, and that is not belt-and-braces. A
# .dockerignore pattern with no leading `**` is anchored to the context ROOT, so a
# bare `.env` excludes only /.env and a bare `dist` excludes only /dist — neither
# touches packages/db/.env, apps/web/.env.local or apps/server/dist, which is
# where this repository's credentials and stale build output actually live. The
# single-form version of this file was written first and verified by building the
# image and listing it: it shipped a developer's .env and a pre-#49 dist/index.js.

# --- Credentials. The load-bearing part of this file ------------------------
# Without these, `COPY . .` bakes a developer's real Supabase and Google
# credentials into a layer that is then pushed to ECR. The `.env.example`
# exceptions mirror .gitignore — templates hold variable names, not values. The
# npm/pnpm rc files are here for the same reason: a registry auth token in one
# would otherwise ride along in a pushed layer.
# The re-includes need BOTH spellings for the same anchoring reason as the
# excludes, and `.env.local.example` needs its own: `*.env.example` requires the
# name to END in `.env.example`, which `.env.local.example` does not — it was
# silently excluded while the comment claimed these mirror .gitignore.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!*.env.example
!**/*.env.example
!*.env.*.example
!**/*.env.*.example
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key

# --- Installed and generated inside the image -------------------------------
# Copying a host node_modules in is both slow and wrong: arm64-vs-x86 native
# binaries, and symlinks into a pnpm store that does not exist in the container.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store

# --- Build output, regenerated inside the image -----------------------------
# A stale host copy is worse than none: `tsc` overwrites what it emits but never
# deletes what it does not, so a leftover dist/index.js from before the module
# reorganisation survives into the image and fails only at container start.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
out
**/out
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Never needed at build or runtime ---------------------------------------
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.github
.vercel
**/.vercel
document
deploy
docker
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
**/Dockerfile
**/README.md
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
